    "reasoning": "1. Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia was suspected due to recent hospitalization but was excluded when “testing for heparin-induced platelet antibody came back negative.” 2. Viral infections (CMV, EBV, HIV) were considered in light of multiorgan involvement but “laboratory studies for underlying infections such as Cytomegalovirus (CMV), Epstein-Barr virus (EBV), Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) were negative.” 3. Autoimmune and other causes of glomerulonephritis were evaluated but autoantibodies (ANA, anti–dsDNA, p-ANCA, c-ANCA) and complement levels “did not show significant results.” 4. Autoimmune pancreatitis was excluded as testing was negative and no imaging abnormalities supported this diagnosis. 5. Alcohol-induced pancreatitis was ruled out by an “undetectable” blood ethanol level. 6. Gallstone pancreatitis was considered given gallbladder sludge but was unlikely since “computed tomography … was unremarkable except for subtle sludge vs gallstones” and “MRCP was unremarkable.”"
  },
